      "sequence_position": 14,
      "problem": "$$\n\nCalculate $\\int \\frac{5x}{4x-4{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x$ for $|x|>1.$",
      "worked_solution": "$$\nThe formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic cotangent function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{5x}{4x-4{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{5x}{4x(1-{x}^{2})}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{5}{4(1-{x}^{2})}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{4}\\int \\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{4}\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
